              The 10-to-14 slide structure is a proven industry standard validated by thousands of funding rounds. However, the difference between a generic presentation and a highly compelling pitch lies in understanding these framework nuances. Founders must master the universal requirements of brevity and problem-solution alignment, while selectively adopting the specific strategies—like Point Nine's rigorous metrics or NextView's conversational appendix—that best fit their company's stage and their target investor's underlying thesis.
            </p>
